---
/**
 * Objection — the customer's own words as a heading, answered with a face and a
 * figure. New at D113.
 *
 * ── WHY IT EXISTS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * The 2026-09-12 research read fifteen well-made sites closely, and the single
 * move every one of them shares is that somewhere it says a sentence that loses
 * it a customer. ONCE: "That's obscene." Plausible's closing call to action:
 * "It's time to ditch Google Analytics." Sivers: "Everything here is 100% me, no
 * AI." Anonymous sites never refuse anything, because a refusal requires a
 * position and a position can be wrong. It costs no color, no motion and no
 * motif, which is why it survived a brief that rules all three out.
 *
 * 37signals heads a section with the buyer's objection verbatim — "But we
 * already have Slack or Teams" — and answers it. This is that shape, aimed at
 * the objection the operator says he actually hears.
 *
 * ── THE OBJECTION IS THE OPERATOR'S, AND SO ARE THE WORDS ───────────────────
 *
 * The first version of this band answered "but my nephew can build me a
 * website", which was Claude's guess at the objection and Claude's wording, and
 * it went live before he had read a word of it. He replaced both: the objection
 * is now the price, and he chose between two drafts with the instruction
 * "Treat this as a decision of mine before publishing."
 *
 * The band is stronger for it. The price box has always been in here, so the
 * money question was already on the page with nothing answering it.
 *
 * ── WHY THE ANSWER CONCEDES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * Because it is true, and because an answer that conceded nothing would be the
 * exact thing this band exists not to be. Sometimes the cheaper quote IS the
 * right answer. Saying so first is what makes the rest of it believable, and it
 * is why the photograph sits beside that opening line rather than above the
 * whole argument.
 *
 * ⚠️ NOTHING HERE MAY READ AS FREE LIFETIME SUPPORT. Upkeep is a PAID monthly
 * arrangement; a page promising the relationship simply continues would
 * contradict the rate sheet a client signs. The copy claims continuity and
 * never claims it is unpriced, and the button goes to `/upkeep/` where the cost
 * of staying is published. That link is the honesty mechanism, not a garnish —
 * do not repoint it at a page with no figure on it.
 *
 * ── WHY THE FACE AND THE FIGURE ARE IN THE SAME BAND ────────────────────────
 *
 * The money question and the trust question are the same question. "Why would I
 * pay you rather than him" is answered by what you get and by who you are
 * dealing with, and splitting those across two sections answers neither.
 *
 * The photograph is the site's first. Getty's VisualGPS work — 7,500 adults per
 * survey across four surveys — puts authentic imagery at the center of trust,
 * and the closest structural competitor found anywhere, one county over, opens
 * his own page with his face. D26 governs what may replace it: a real capture,
 * never a generated image.
 *
 * THE FIGURE IS DERIVED AND ITS QUALIFIER TRAVELS INSIDE THE SAME BOX. D5 as
 * amended requires the two to appear together; putting them in one bordered
 * object makes that structural rather than something a future editor remembers.
 * Never type the number here — `npm run gate` refuses a hand-typed price, and it
 * separately refuses a build where nothing renders one.
 */
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import Button from '../Button.astro';
import { versioned } from '../../data/asset-version';
import { objection } from '../../data/home';
import { FLOOR_USD, FLOOR_QUALIFIER } from '../../lib/pricing.js';
import { money } from '../../lib/format.js';
---
<Section width="popout">
  <h2 class="refusal">{objection.heading}</h2>

  {/* THE FACE SITS WITH THE FIRST PARAGRAPH, NOT ABOVE THE WHOLE ANSWER. The
      first line is the concession — the one place on the page where he agrees
      the customer might be right — and that is the sentence a photograph should
      be attached to. The rest of the argument runs full width beneath it. */}
  <div class="mt-7 flex flex-col gap-5 sm:flex-row sm:items-start sm:gap-6">
    <img
      class="portrait"
      src={versioned(objection.portrait)}
      alt={objection.portraitAlt}
      width="132"
      height="132"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
    />
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{objection.body[0]}</p>
  </div>

  {objection.body.slice(1).map((para) => (
    <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">{para}</p>
  ))}

  <div class="pricebox mt-7">
    <div class="pricebox-head">
      <p class="mono-label">{objection.priceLabel}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pricebox-body">
      <p class="pricebox-figure">{money(FLOOR_USD)}</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        {FLOOR_QUALIFIER} The first conversation is free either way.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-7">
    <Button href={objection.cta.href} variant="secondary">{objection.cta.label}</Button>
  </div>
</Section>
